# MIGRATION 2.2.1 -> 2.3 (tally 2.3, #247; the review of G3, Q5): a leftover `one_of` in an observation's
# attribute prints what an unknown word prints there, `LOAD-UNIT a value of the wrong type`. Before: W3's own
# words.
=== m.tally
model ob
  tally 2
  on 2026-08-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source s "invented"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
kind wages: event certain
  leg cash: PLN
  attr period: date
  attr cnt: int
input bank: observed
version st
  cite s
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-04-02
  covers konto
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"
  bank[r1] = (on: 2026-03-10, kind: wages, leg cash from world to konto amount 50.00 PLN, period: one_of([2026-04-06, 2026-04-13]), cnt: 3) "r1"
=== expect
refused: LOAD-UNIT a value of the wrong type for bank[r1] (m.tally:21)
